{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1194396-orichalcum-prayer-beads-of-enlightenment-zenyatta-s-orbs","id":1194396,"title":"Orichalcum Prayer Beads of Enlightenment - Zenyatta's Orbs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-11T17:09:12-07:00","id":1194396,"title":"Orichalcum Prayer Beads of Enlightenment - Zenyatta's Orbs","content":"Gauging forum interest in this project.<br /> <br /> Light Artifact Throwing weapon. No Hearthstone slot. Primarily orichalcum, with moonsilver and starmetal for flavor.<br /> <br /> Upon attuning to these eight spheres, they levitate around the user's neck, requiring no hands to hold. They can be readied for combat reflexively, but require at a free hand to launch one. Using a Ready Weapon action recalls all fired spheres, which teleport back to the user.<br /> <br /> The first and perhaps only attack Evocation would be Orb of Destruction, which upgrades the use of Cascade of Cutting Terror, perhaps improving that Charm's performance based on how many prayer beads you still have ready, and explicitly letting that Charm reset when you use the Ready Weapon recall action to recall all of the beads.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next Evocation is Orb of Harmony, which sends a sphere to another character to orbit around their head. It might provide them with a Passion of Hope, Joy, Reassurance, or similar positive emotion that they might be able to use to boost their Resolve against appropriate social influence or providing an avenue for the monk's Persuade attempts. Leaving a bead floating around someone else means you can't use it to attack, but you can choose to leave it with them when recalling the others.<br /> <br /> From this Evocation would come Solar-specific Evocations that make the orb a channel for Presence Charms.<ul><li>Empowering Shout \u2013 reduces the mote cost by 1 if the orb was attached to the subject before the current round.</li> <li>Favor-Conferring Prana, Underling-Promoting Touch \u2013 waives the willpower cost, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached</li> <li>Divinity-Conferring Touch \u2013 halves the mote cost, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached</li> <li>Shedding Infinite Radiance \u2013 can perform the dramatic action within one turn of combat, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached</li> </ul>Another would allow the Solar to target the orb's subject with the following Lore Charms: Essence-Lending Method, Will-Bolstering Method, and Wound-Accepting Technique.<br /> <br /> Another would allow the Solar to target the orb's subject with Medicine Charms that instantly take effect, such as Touch of Blissful Release and Anointment of Miraculous Health. If the Solar knows Instant Treatment Methodology, medical treatment actions through the Orb of Harmony become possible. Using Instant Treatment Methodology likewise enables the use of Medicine Charms that replace treatment actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Transcendance&quot; requires the Solar to know the pinnacle Integrity Charm, Inviolable Essence Merging. The Evocation empowers the Orbs to use the Solar's traits -- including her Charms -- to minister to others for as long as she meditates in their presence. This by itself doesn't allow the Solar to float around anywhere, doesn't provide an increase in speed, and certainly doesn't avoid IEM's restriction against attacking or harming others prior to meditation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Discord Orb might inflict a Passion of Despair, Doubt, Sadness, or Fear upon the target, penalizing their Resolve against appropriate social influence and providing an avenue for the monk to perform Persuade attempts.<br /> <br /> Evocations would allow the long-range use of Injury-Forcing Technique and Essence-Draining Touch, and assist in the use of Will-Shattering Illusion and the Solar Presence Charms, Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment and Holy Touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-11-2018, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T09:50:32-07:00","id":1194562,"title":"","content":"I like this idea actually!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13595-yawgrimas","name":"Yawgrimas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T18:21:32-07:00","id":1194684,"title":"","content":"Seconded! I'd love too see this, and one of my players might even use it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T07:54:21-07:00","id":1195297,"title":"","content":"Reminds me a bit of Okami's bead weapons, because of that I was half expecting the beads be able to be used all at once as pseudo whip like in that game.<br /> How large are these spheres?<br /> If they are small enough I can actually imagine someone trying to load them into the barrel of fire wand.<br /> Or if they are too large for that, I'm imagining someone using their Diremaul like a bat ( or racket or croquet hammer) etc. to smash those balls into their enemies.<br /> <br /> Sure it may be unconventional usage but it would be a fun way to create some cross artifact evocations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T08:46:15-07:00","id":1195313,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/overwatch/images/f/f5/Zenyatta_portrait.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/350?cb=20160429042336\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> They're about fist-sized in the inspiration.<br /> <br /> Also I think he actually has nine of them. (in this picture one is possibly hidden behind his head)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-14-2018, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:23:41-07:00","id":1195326,"title":"","content":"Amaterasu\u2019s magatama prayer beads are a similar but different sort of weapon, with a different focus. For one thing, they are far more destructive, and would probably \u201cpurify\u201d creatures of darkness, spirits, and other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> Watching Zenyatta\u2019s dance emote confirms that he has nine orbs. Amusingly, his ammo count is apparently 20 orbs, even after he\u2019s tagged a Harmony Orb and a Discord Orb on people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:10:04-07:00","id":1195410,"title":"","content":"not a bad idea<br /> <br /> I would add an evocation that would allow you to use an aim action to charge up a magical flurry that sends Essence number of orbs hurdling towards the target - for massive damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:23:32-07:00","id":1195523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1194396-orichalcum-prayer-beads-of-enlightenment-zenyatta-s-orbs?p=1195410#post1195410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not a bad idea<br /> <br /> I would add an evocation that would allow you to use an aim action to charge up a magical flurry that sends Essence number of orbs hurdling towards the target - for massive damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read the fourth paragraph?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:57:13-07:00","id":1196535,"title":"","content":"<b>ORBS OF DESTRUCTION<br /> Cost: </b>5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> After taking an Aim action against an enemy, the monk can use use this Charm to fire all remaining orbs at a target. For each orb fired, the attack enjoys one bonus die to the attack (subject to the monk's inherent dice-adding limits) and the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> How's that look? A toned-down version of Cascade of Cutting Terror, for singular targets and more frequent use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T06:00:27-07:00","id":1201898,"title":"","content":"<b>ORB OF HARMONY</b><br /> <i>1m; Simple; Indefinite; </i><i>Decisive-only</i><i>; Essence 1; No Prerequisites</i><br /> <br /> The monk casts an orb at an ally within long range. Targeting an unwilling subject out of battle requires an opposed roll, and in battle requires a Difficulty 2 gambit. If it succeeds, the sphere orbits around their head and draws out their most positive thoughts and memories. In effect, it provides them with a Passion of Hope, Joy, Reassurance, or similar positive emotion that they might be able to use to boost their Resolve against appropriate social influence. This Passion also provides an avenue for the monk's own social influence attempts, and the bonus is instead applied as a penalty to the subject\u2019s Guile for the monk\u2019s attempts to glean the thoughts or Intimacies which the orb is strengthening.<br /> <br /> The monk may bless as many subjects as he has orbs and motes to commit, though he cannot bless an individual with more than one orb. While the orb remains with a subject, the monk cannot use it to attack. The monk need not recall the orb when recalling orbs he has used to attack. If the subject enters extreme range or breaks line of sight for more than one round, the orb reflexively returns on its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HARMONIOUS ENCOURAGEMENT</b><br /> <i>No Cost; Permanent; No Keywords; Essence 2; Orb of Harmony, Empowering Shout</i><br /> <br /> When the Solar is blessing an individual with an Orb of Harmony, he enjoys additional benefits to using the following Charms upon them:<br /> <br /> <i>Empowering Shout</i> \u2013 reduces the mote cost by 1 if the orb was attached to the subject before the current round.<br /> <i>Favor-Conferring Prana </i>\u2013 waives the willpower cost, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached<br /> <i>Underling-Promoting Touch</i> \u2013 waives the willpower cost, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached<br /> <i>Divinity-Conferring Touch</i> \u2013 halves the mote cost, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached<br /> <i>Shedding Infinite Radiance</i> \u2013 can perform the dramatic action within one turn of combat, but the effect only lasts as long as the orb is attached<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HARMONIOUS HEALING</b><br /> <i>No Cost; Permanent; No Keywords; Essence 2; Orb of Harmony, Instant Treatment Methodology or Touch of Blissful Release</i><br /> <br /> When the Solar is blessing an individual with an Orb of Harmony, he may target them from afar with any Medicine Charms which take effect instantly, such as Touch of Blissful Release.<br /> <br /> If the Solar knows Flawless Diagnosis Technique, he may perform a diagnosis action from afar, and enjoys +1 success when conventionally diagnosing the patient more closely.<br /> <br /> If the Solar knows Instant Treatment Methodology, he may use that Charm to perform medical treatment actions from afar, and use Medicine Charms which take the form of medical treatment actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HARMONIOUS EMPOWERMENT</b><br /> <i>No Cost; Permanent; No Keywords; Essence 2; Orb of Harmony, Essence-Lending Method</i><br /> <br /> When the Solar is blessing an individual with an Orb of Harmony, he may target them with Essence-Lending Method, Will-Bolstering Technique, or Wound-Accepting Technique without needing to touch them.<br /> <br /> If the Solar is blessing all allies she wishes to affect with Power-Restoring Invocation, she waives the Charm\u2019s Initiative point cost.<br /> <br /> If the Solar knows Surging Essence Flow, her orbs may continue to bless an individual even if they spend an hour outside of her line of sight, though they must remain within long range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-01-2018, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T06:19:26-07:00","id":1201900,"title":"","content":"Removing an Orb of Harmony or Discord from one's self or another character requires a Decisive attack which scores (monk's Essence + 2) successes on the damage roll. The Orb's Defense is equal to the monk's Essence rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ORB OF DISCORD</b><br /> <i>2m; Simple; Indefinite; Decisive-only; Essence 2; Orb of Destruction, Orb of Harmony</i><br /> <br /> The monk casts an orb at an individual within long range. If this does not provoke a battle, the action requires an opposed roll. If it does, or the two characters are already rolled into battle, it requires a Difficulty 2 gambit. If it succeeds, the sphere orbits around their head and draws out their most negative thoughts and memories. In effect, it provides them with a Passion of Despair, Sorrow, Regret, Anger, or similar negative emotion that they might be able to use to boost their Resolve against appropriate social influence, or that others might use against them. The penalty of the Passion is applied to the subject\u2019s Guile for the monk\u2019s attempts to glean the thoughts or Intimacies which the orb is strengthening.<br /> <br /> The monk may burden as many subjects as he has orbs and motes to commit, though he cannot burden an individual with more than one orb. While the orb remains with a subject, the monk cannot use it to attack. The monk need not recall the orb when recalling orbs he has used to attack. If the subject enters extreme range or breaks line of sight for more than one round, the orb reflexively returns on its own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PAIN IS AN EXCELLENT TEACHER</b><br /> <i>No Cost; Permanent; No Keywords; Essence 3; Orb of Harmony, Injury-Forcing Technique or Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment</i><br /> <br /> When the Solar is burdening an individual with an Orb of Discord, he may target them with Injury-Forcing Technique, Essence-Draining Touch, and Holy Touch without needing to touch them. When using Holy Touch, the target is always pushed away from the monk.<br /> <br /> The cost of Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment against that subject is reduced by 2 motes.<br /> <br /> The penalty of the negative Passion inspired by the Discord Orb applies to their roll to resist Will-Shattering Illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-01-2018, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T10:20:49-07:00","id":1201958,"title":"","content":"I'm not bumping this thread because of some April's Fools joke.<br /> <br /> I'm actually posting the Evocations of the Artifact you all said you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T10:58:55-07:00","id":1201966,"title":"","content":"I like the overall flavor. An explict statement on the number of orbs would help me gauge Orbs of Destruction better. The use of them as social tools is novel and cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T11:22:23-07:00","id":1201971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1194396-orichalcum-prayer-beads-of-enlightenment-zenyatta-s-orbs?p=1201966#post1201966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the overall flavor. An explict statement on the number of orbs would help me gauge Orbs of Destruction better. The use of them as social tools is novel and cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>ZENYATTA\u2019S PRAYER BEADS OF ENLIGHTENMENT (Orichalcum Prayer Beads, Rating 3)</b><br /> <b>Attunement:</b> 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Light (Damage + 10, Overwhelming 3)<br /> <b>Tags: </b>Bashing, Thrown (Medium)<br /> <b>Hearthstone Slot(s):</b> None<br /> <b>Era:</b> ???<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement Bonus:</b><br /> Nine beads, nine shots. Getting them to float around your neck indefinite requires a Draw Weapon action, but afterwards you don't need a Draw Weapon action to use them. Doesn\u2019t need hands to hold but needs an empty hand to shoot. Can recall any or all of the beads with a single Draw Weapon action.<br /> <br /> Normal max range is Medium. Sending them out as far as the Long range allowed by the Evocations requires a range-extending effect, though the subject of the orb can wander out that far without anything special from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:56:31-07:00","id":1212618,"title":"","content":"Who wants Zenyatta's Prayer Beads of Enlightenment in jade form, for Dragon-Blooded?<br /> <br /> Like, ten orbs; two of each color of jade.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: The joke is going to be on y'all if any of you would really want this artifact, but no one reads this post because no one thinks I might have a good reason to bump the thread.<br /> <br /> I've got enough projects to do. I don't need to do this one, even for my own entertainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-28-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T13:02:50-07:00","id":1212768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1194396-orichalcum-prayer-beads-of-enlightenment-zenyatta-s-orbs?p=1212618#post1212618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who wants Zenyatta's Prayer Beads of Enlightenment in jade form, for Dragon-Blooded?<br /> <br /> Like, ten orbs; two of each color of jade.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: The joke is going to be on y'all if any of you would really want this artifact, but no one reads this post because no one thinks I might have a good reason to bump the thread.<br /> <br /> I've got enough projects to do. I don't need to do this one, even for my own entertainment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It could be neat, but I don't know if it'd really add anything to it. The Dragonblooded still use Orichalcum for things, so even the bass artifact is fitting for a powerful Immaculate monk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T14:01:36-07:00","id":1212789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1194396-orichalcum-prayer-beads-of-enlightenment-zenyatta-s-orbs?p=1212768#post1212768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\